# This repo is edited on Windows and served as static files by Netlify, which is
# indifferent to line endings. Store every file byte-for-byte as it sits on disk
# (CRLF) so git never rewrites endings behind our backs.
#
# Why -text rather than "text=auto eol=crlf": the repo was already mixed. app.js,
# index.html, sw.js and manifest.json were committed as CRLF; the rest as LF.
# Normalising to LF would rewrite app.js entirely -- the one file every upgrade
# phase edits. This way app.js, index.html and sw.js are left untouched and only
# the already-drifted files are restated.
* -text
